# Locked HR UI — ask before changing

These surfaces are **frozen by product decision**. Files contain `LOCKED UI` comments marking the exact blocks.

## Canonical standards

1. **Company HR Policies** (`HrPoliciesForm.tsx`) — typography scale for HR settings forms:
   - Section headers: `text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide`
   - Field labels: `text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500`
   - Helpers: `text-[10px]` / `text-[11px] text-slate-400`
   - Inputs: `h-9 text-sm`

2. **Employee Register** (`employees-page.tsx` + filters + columns) — also the **app-wide list toolbar standard**:
   - Shared: `components/list-toolbar.tsx` (`ListToolbar`, `ListSearchField`, `ListToolbarSelect`, `FilterChipGroup`)
   - Toolbar: search (pill) → All departments → status chips
   - Chips: All / Active / Probation / On leave / Exiting / Inactive
   - Active chip: `bg-slate-900 text-white`; idle: white + `border-slate-200`
   - Columns: Employee (name+code), Status, Nationality, Department/Division, Designation, Joined
   - Other list pages should reuse these primitives rather than inventing new search/chip styles

3. **Home module cards** (`dashboard.tsx` Modules tab):
   - Compact previous size: `items-start`, `p-3.5`, natural height, description `line-clamp-2` (no forced `min-h` / `auto-rows-fr`)
   - Layout: icon | title + blurb | arrow in `lg:grid-cols-4`

3b. **KPI / summary cards** (`summary-card.tsx` + `kpi-summary-strip.tsx`):
   - Same compact scale as home tiles: `p-3.5`, `gap-3`, `h-9 w-9` icon, value `text-lg` (not `text-2xl` / `py-5`)

4. **Reporting Manager list** (`CurrentJobForm.tsx`):
   - Same department as the job being edited
   - Plus company `ceoEmployeeId`
   - Plus titles matching CEO / Chief Executive / Managing Director
   - Always keep the currently saved manager visible

## Agent requirement

Before restyling, renaming chips, changing column layout, altering this typography, changing module-card height, or broadening the reporting-manager list:

1. **Stop and ask the user** whether they want to change the locked pattern.
2. Do not “improve” or normalize these areas to match other modules without explicit approval.
3. Bug fixes that preserve visual design are OK (logic, data, a11y) without asking.
